<section id="questionnaires">
  <h2>A day of compliance work, done in 30 minutes</h2>
  <p class="sum">An AI pipeline that drafts answers to client security questionnaires from a curated evidence library, with a person approving every answer.</p>
  <figure>
    <div class="scroll" tabindex="0"><svg viewBox="0 0 760 220" role="img" aria-label="Questionnaire flow: parse and redact, search evidence, draft with sources, human review, export"><defs><marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="ahp"/></marker></defs><g class="n ext"><rect x="0.0" y="40" width="112" height="64" rx="6"/><text x="56.0" y="68.5">Client</text><text x="56.0" y="83.5">questionnaire</text></g><g class="n"><rect x="129.6" y="40" width="112" height="64" rx="6"/><text x="185.6" y="68.5">Parse and</text><text x="185.6" y="83.5">redact</text></g><path class="e" d="M112.0,72.0 L127.6,72.0" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><g class="n"><rect x="259.2" y="40" width="112" height="64" rx="6"/><text x="315.2" y="68.5">Search evidence</text><text x="315.2" y="83.5">library (MCP)</text></g><path class="e" d="M241.6,72.0 L257.2,72.0" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><g class="n model"><rect x="388.79999999999995" y="40" width="112" height="64" rx="6"/><text x="444.79999999999995" y="68.5">Draft answers</text><text x="444.79999999999995" y="83.5">with sources</text></g><path class="e" d="M371.2,72.0 L386.79999999999995,72.0" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><g class="n human"><rect x="518.4" y="40" width="112" height="64" rx="14"/><text x="574.4" y="68.5">Person reviews</text><text x="574.4" y="83.5">and approves</text></g><path class="e" d="M500.79999999999995,72.0 L516.4,72.0" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><g class="n"><rect x="648.0" y="40" width="112" height="64" rx="6"/><text x="704.0" y="68.5">Export to</text><text x="704.0" y="83.5">client format</text></g><path class="e" d="M630.4,72.0 L646.0,72.0" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><g class="n store"><path d="M259.2,158 a56.0,8 0 0,0 112,0 v42 a56.0,8 0 0,1 -112,0 z"/><ellipse cx="315.2" cy="158" rx="56.0" ry="8"/><text x="315.2" y="179.5">Evidence</text><text x="315.2" y="194.5">library</text></g><path class="e" d="M315.2,150 L315.2,107" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><text class="cap" x="383.2" y="184">15 owned sections, reviewed quarterly</text><text class="cap" x="185.6" y="26" text-anchor="middle">sensitive data removed before any model call</text></svg></div>
    <figcaption>The model only drafts. Nothing leaves the building without a reviewer's approval, and sensitive data is stripped before any model sees it.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <h3>The problem</h3>
  <p>Institutional clients send long due-diligence questionnaires, each in its own format. Answering one took about a full day of searching old answers and policy documents, and the evidence lived in an unstructured 67 MB pile of files.</p>
  <h3>What I did</h3>
  <p>I fixed the data before automating anything. I reorganized the evidence into 15 sections, each with an owner and a quarterly review. Then I built a portal that parses questionnaires from 6+ client formats, redacts sensitive data, searches the evidence through an MCP server, and drafts answers with their sources attached. People review, edit and approve each one.</p>
  <h3>Results</h3>
  <ul class="results">
    <li>Turnaround dropped from about a day to 30–45 minutes.</li>
    <li>The people who did this by hand say it made the whole process easier to manage, start to finish.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="stack"><strong>Stack:</strong> Python, FastAPI, React and TypeScript, MCP, Anthropic API. About 17,000 lines.</p>
</section>

<section id="helpdesk">
  <h2>A help desk agent that asks before it acts</h2>
  <p class="sum">An interactive agent in Microsoft Teams that answers IT questions from the company knowledge base and past tickets, and opens a ticket only when the person says yes.</p>
  <figure>
    <div class="scroll" tabindex="0"><svg viewBox="0 0 760 262" role="img" aria-label="Help desk agent: answers from knowledge base and resolved tickets; opens a ticket only after the employee confirms"><defs><marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="ahp"/></marker></defs><g class="n ext"><rect x="0" y="70" width="120" height="60" rx="6"/><text x="60.0" y="96.5">Employee in</text><text x="60.0" y="111.5">Teams chat</text></g><g class="n model"><rect x="190" y="70" width="150" height="60" rx="6"/><text x="265.0" y="96.5">Help desk agent</text><text x="265.0" y="111.5">(Bedrock AgentCore)</text></g><g class="n store"><path d="M420,8 a75.0,8 0 0,0 150,0 v38 a75.0,8 0 0,1 -150,0 z"/><ellipse cx="495.0" cy="8" rx="75.0" ry="8"/><text x="495.0" y="27.5">Knowledge</text><text x="495.0" y="42.5">base</text></g><g class="n store"><path d="M420,154 a75.0,8 0 0,0 150,0 v38 a75.0,8 0 0,1 -150,0 z"/><ellipse cx="495.0" cy="154" rx="75.0" ry="8"/><text x="495.0" y="173.5">Resolved</text><text x="495.0" y="188.5">tickets index</text></g><g class="n human"><rect x="620" y="70" width="140" height="60" rx="14"/><text x="690.0" y="96.5">Employee confirms</text><text x="690.0" y="111.5">the ticket</text></g><g class="n"><rect x="620" y="196" width="140" height="54" rx="6"/><text x="690.0" y="219.5">Service desk</text><text x="690.0" y="234.5">ticket created</text></g><path class="e" d="M120,92 L188,92" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><text class="el" x="154" y="84">question</text><path class="e" d="M190,112 L122,112" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><text class="el" x="156" y="128">answer</text><path class="e" d="M340,86 C380,86 380,27 418,27" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><path class="e" d="M340,114 C380,114 380,173 418,173" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><text class="el" x="372" y="52">retrieve</text><path class="e dash" d="M340,100 L618,100" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><text class="el" x="480" y="94">proposes a ticket</text><path class="e" d="M690,130 L690,194" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><text class="el" x="700" y="166" style="text-anchor:start">only if yes</text></svg></div>
    <figcaption>Answers come from retrieval over real documentation and resolved tickets. Taking an action, opening a service-desk ticket, always waits for the employee's confirmation.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <h3>The problem</h3>
  <p>A small IT team spent a lot of time on questions that had already been answered, in the knowledge base or in old tickets.</p>
  <h3>What I did</h3>
  <p>I built a retrieval agent on AWS Bedrock AgentCore over the structured knowledge base and an index of 2,454 resolved tickets. When it can't solve something, it drafts a ticket and asks the employee to confirm before creating it. All of the infrastructure is code.</p>
  <h3>Results</h3>
  <ul class="results">
    <li>Working prototype in 10 days, then approved as a formal project.</li>
    <li>Redesigned the ticket sync so each run makes about 20 API calls instead of about 2,450.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="stack"><strong>Stack:</strong> AWS Bedrock AgentCore and Knowledge Bases, OpenSearch Serverless, Lambda, EventBridge, Terraform (about 3,800 lines across 6 stacks), Microsoft Teams.</p>
</section>

<section id="gateway">
  <h2>Safe AI access for a whole company</h2>
  <p class="sum">One governed path from every AI tool to the models, so a finance company could adopt AI without sending data where it shouldn't go.</p>
  <figure>
    <div class="scroll" tabindex="0"><svg viewBox="0 0 760 260" role="img" aria-label="Company AI access: all tools route through a governed gateway to models in a private cloud account"><defs><marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="ahp"/></marker></defs><g class="n ext"><rect x="0" y="10" width="150" height="52" rx="6"/><text x="75.0" y="32.5">Desktop and</text><text x="75.0" y="47.5">coding assistants</text></g><g class="n ext"><rect x="0" y="84" width="150" height="52" rx="6"/><text x="75.0" y="106.5">Internal apps</text><text x="75.0" y="121.5">and agents</text></g><g class="n ext"><rect x="0" y="158" width="150" height="52" rx="6"/><text x="75.0" y="180.5">Automation</text><text x="75.0" y="195.5">scripts</text></g><g class="n human"><rect x="260" y="60" width="190" height="100" rx="14"/><text x="355.0" y="99.0">LLM gateway</text><text x="355.0" y="114.0">keys, budgets, logging,</text><text x="355.0" y="129.0">approved models only</text></g><g class="n model"><rect x="560" y="60" width="200" height="100" rx="6"/><text x="660.0" y="106.5">Models in the company&#x27;s</text><text x="660.0" y="121.5">private cloud account</text></g><path class="e" d="M150,36 C205,36 205,110 258,110" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><path class="e" d="M150,110 C205,110 205,110 258,110" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><path class="e" d="M150,184 C205,184 205,110 258,110" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><path class="e" d="M450,110 L558,110" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><g class="n"><rect x="260" y="196" width="190" height="52" rx="6"/><text x="355.0" y="218.5">Approved MCP</text><text x="355.0" y="233.5">server catalogue</text></g><path class="e dash" d="M355,196 L355,163" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><text class="el" x="366" y="184" style="text-anchor:start">vetted tools</text></svg></div>
    <figcaption>Every request goes through one gateway that holds the keys, enforces budgets, logs usage and only allows approved models running in the company's own cloud account.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <h3>What I did</h3>
  <p>I led the company's rollout of Claude. I routed model traffic through an internal LiteLLM gateway to AWS Bedrock, solved running the desktop and coding assistants on virtual desktops, and packaged an installer for managed laptops. I also keep the catalogue of MCP servers people are approved to use.</p>
  <p class="stack"><strong>Stack:</strong> LiteLLM, AWS Bedrock, Claude, MCP, Cloudflare Zero Trust, Intune.</p>
</section>

<section id="publishing">
  <h2>When the right answer isn't AI</h2>
  <p class="sum">A web app that replaced a Word document for the company's standard due-diligence questionnaire, with versioned publishing and a tamper-evident audit trail.</p>
  <figure>
    <div class="scroll" tabindex="0"><svg viewBox="0 0 760 210" role="img" aria-label="Questionnaire site: drafts are published as versions, every change is written to a hash-chained audit log"><defs><marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="ahp"/></marker></defs><g class="n ext"><rect x="0" y="30" width="140" height="60" rx="6"/><text x="70.0" y="56.5">Admin edits</text><text x="70.0" y="71.5">a draft</text></g><g class="n human"><rect x="200" y="30" width="150" height="60" rx="14"/><text x="275.0" y="56.5">Publish as a</text><text x="275.0" y="71.5">new version</text></g><g class="n"><rect x="410" y="30" width="150" height="60" rx="6"/><text x="485.0" y="56.5">Published</text><text x="485.0" y="71.5">version</text></g><g class="n ext"><rect x="620" y="30" width="140" height="60" rx="6"/><text x="690.0" y="56.5">Client downloads</text><text x="690.0" y="71.5">PDF or Word</text></g><path class="e" d="M140,60 L198,60" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><path class="e" d="M350,60 L408,60" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><path class="e" d="M560,60 L618,60" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><g class="n store"><path d="M200,148 a75.0,8 0 0,0 150,0 v44 a75.0,8 0 0,1 -150,0 z"/><ellipse cx="275.0" cy="148" rx="75.0" ry="8"/><text x="275.0" y="170.5">Append-only</text><text x="275.0" y="185.5">audit log</text></g><g class="n store"><path d="M410,148 a75.0,8 0 0,0 150,0 v44 a75.0,8 0 0,1 -150,0 z"/><ellipse cx="485.0" cy="148" rx="75.0" ry="8"/><text x="485.0" y="170.5">Version history</text><text x="485.0" y="185.5">with rollback</text></g><path class="e dash" d="M275,90 L275,138" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><path class="e dash" d="M485,90 L485,138" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><text class="el" x="285" y="120" style="text-anchor:start">every change recorded</text><text class="cap" x="30" y="166">each entry is hash-chained</text><text class="cap" x="30" y="182">to the one before it</text></svg></div>
    <figcaption>Admins edit drafts in the browser and publish them as versions. Every change goes into an append-only log where each entry is hash-chained to the last, so the history can't be quietly rewritten.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <h3>The problem</h3>
  <p>The company's standard answers to client due-diligence questions lived in a Word file. Keeping it current, knowing which version a client had received, and proving who changed what were all manual.</p>
  <h3>What I did</h3>
  <p>I built a web app where admins edit the questionnaire in the browser, move it from draft to published, and roll back to any earlier version. Clients download the latest version as a generated PDF or Word file. This problem needed reliable software and an audit trail, not a model, so it has none.</p>
</section>

<section id="how">
  <h2>How I work</h2>
  <p class="sum">Claude Code is my main development tool. In 2026 I used it on about 70 projects, from full-stack internal apps to cloud migrations. I treat its output the way I'd treat a sharp new teammate's.</p>
  <ul class="habits">
    <li><strong>Nothing ships unreviewed.</strong> AI-written changes go through the same gates as mine: infrastructure plans, dry runs and code review. Dry runs once caught two fleet-wide failures before release, one that would have stopped a management agent on every server and one that would have reset certificates on 40 hosts at once.</li>
    <li><strong>Fix the data first.</strong> A well-organized source beats a clever prompt.</li>
    <li><strong>Use AI where it earns its place.</strong> Plenty of problems need a script, an automation rule or a scheduled job, and I build those too.</li>
    <li><strong>Put the guardrail in the system.</strong> Confirmation steps, read-only roles and redaction hold up better than instructions in a prompt.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

